  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Atomics Aeronautical Systems obligated $1.3B in FY2026 to date. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems received 162 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $8.2M. Obligations fell 19.0% year over year. Department of Defense leads buying activity, obligating $1B, followed by Department of Homeland Security with $314M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for General Atomics Aeronautical Systems at $524M, followed by Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $315M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $228M. Historical obligations show year-to-year variation: FY21 $2B, FY22 $1.9B, FY23 $1.8B, FY24 $2.3B, FY25 $1.6B, FY26 $1.3B. Industry-level awards include Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $152M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $68.8M. Small-value markets include All Other Support Services at $348K, Flight Training at $312K, Engineering Services at $111K, and Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $39.3K. Figures are contract obligations except where noted as total contract values.",
